### ============================================
### Authentication API - /auth Controller
### HTTP Requests to test login and registration
### ============================================

### Variables (adjust as needed)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### NOTES:
### - The project includes sample users initialized by DataInitializer:
###   - john.doe@example.com (password: A1234567)
###   - jane.smith@example.com (password: B1234567)
### - Available endpoints in AuthController:
###   POST /auth/login
###   POST /auth/register

### ============================================
### 1. LOGIN (POST) - Authenticate user
### ============================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "A1234567"
}

### Expected response: AuthResponse (token, expiresAt, userId) depending on implementation


### ============================================
### 2. REGISTER USER (POST)
### ============================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "documentNumber": "3333333",
  "name": "Carlos",
  "firstName": "González",
  "lastName": "Lopez",
  "email": "carlos.gonzalez@example.com",
  "password": "C1234567",
  "phoneNumber": "3007654321",
  "birthDate": "1995-04-20"
}

### Expected response: UUID of the created user (201 Created)


### ============================================
### 3. FULL FLOW TEST: Register then login
### ============================================

# 1) Register a new user
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "documentNumber": "4444444",
  "name": "Test",
  "firstName": "User",
  "lastName": "Example",
  "email": "test.user@example.com",
  "password": "T1234567",
  "phoneNumber": "3000000001",
  "birthDate": "1990-01-01"
}

###
# 2) Login with the newly created user
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test.user@example.com",
  "password": "T1234567"
}
